/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Revelation chapters 16-20
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("revelation", [
{n:16, name:"The Seven Vials",
 seal:{ref:"Revelation 16:15",verse:"Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments, lest he walk naked, and they see his shame."},
 facts:["Did you know Armageddon comes from Hebrew for the mountain of Megiddo, a real ancient battlefield, and here it is the gathering place for the kings of the whole world (Revelation 16:16)?","Did you know each hailstone in the last plague weighs about a talent, roughly what a strong man could carry, which is why the plague is called exceeding great (Revelation 16:21)?","Did you know the seven vials echo the plagues of Egypt? Blood, darkness, and sores fall again, and again the sufferers harden their hearts and refuse to repent (Revelation 16:9, 11)."],
 questions:[
{q:"Who ordered the seven angels to pour out their vials?", options:["A great voice out of the temple","The four beasts","The elders on the thrones","John himself"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:1",verse:"And I heard a great voice out of the temple saying to the seven angels, Go your ways, and pour out the vials of the wrath of God upon the earth.", insight:"The command comes from the temple itself; judgment is issued from God's own house, not man's anger."},
{q:"Where did the first angel pour out his vial?", options:["Upon the earth","Upon the sea","Upon the sun","Into the air"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:2",verse:"And the first went, and poured out his vial upon the earth; and there fell a noisome and grievous sore upon the men which had the mark of the beast, and upon them which worshipped his image.", insight:"The plague begins at everyone's feet; none of us can lift ourselves above God's reach."},
{q:"What fell upon the men who had the mark of the beast?", options:["A noisome and grievous sore","Blindness for three days","A consuming fever","Leprosy like snow"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:2",verse:"And the first went, and poured out his vial upon the earth; and there fell a noisome and grievous sore upon the men which had the mark of the beast, and upon them which worshipped his image.", insight:"The mark men took to save their lives becomes the mark of their misery; sin keeps no bargains."},
{q:"What did the sea become when the second angel poured out his vial?", options:["As the blood of a dead man","Like burning oil","As dark as the pit","Dry like a desert"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:3",verse:"And the second angel poured out his vial upon the sea; and it became as the blood of a dead man: and every living soul died in the sea.", insight:"The sea that carried their trade becomes death itself; God's judgments reach the highways of wealth."},
{q:"What happened to every living soul in the sea?", options:["It died","It fled to shore","It turned to stone","It was carried into the deep"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:3",verse:"And the second angel poured out his vial upon the sea; and it became as the blood of a dead man: and every living soul died in the sea.", insight:"Total and final; when God judges, He does not leave room for half measures."},
{q:"Upon what did the third angel pour out his vial?", options:["The rivers and fountains of waters","The wells of the desert","The pools of the city","The springs of the mountains"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:4",verse:"And the third angel poured out his vial upon the rivers and fountains of waters; and they became blood.", insight:"Even the sweet fountains turn to blood; no source of life outside God stays sweet forever."},
{q:"How did the angel of the waters describe the Lord?", options:["Righteous, which art, and wast, and shalt be","Merciful and slow to wrath","Hidden from the eyes of men","Silent before the wicked"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:5",verse:"And I heard the angel of the waters say, Thou art righteous, O Lord, which art, and wast, and shalt be, because thou hast judged thus.", insight:"Heaven itself defends God's justice; His past, present, and future are all righteous."},
{q:"Why were the wicked given blood to drink?", options:["They had shed the blood of saints and prophets","They had polluted the wells","They had refused the water of life","They had worshipped the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:6",verse:"For they have shed the blood of saints and prophets, and thou hast given them blood to drink; for they are worthy.", insight:"'They are worthy'; God measures the judgment to the crime with terrible exactness."},
{q:"What did the voice out of the altar say about God's judgments?", options:["True and righteous are thy judgments","Too severe for the crime","Hidden from the saints","Delayed past their time"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:7",verse:"And I heard another out of the altar say, Even so, Lord God Almighty, true and righteous are thy judgments.", insight:"Even the altar of sacrifice agrees; heaven finds no fault in God's justice."},
{q:"Upon what did the fourth angel pour out his vial?", options:["Upon the sun","Upon the moon","Upon the stars","Upon the firmament"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:8",verse:"And the fourth angel poured out his vial upon the sun; and power was given unto him to scorch men with fire.", insight:"The sun that once warmed their harvests becomes their tormentor; blessings turn when God is forgotten."},
{q:"How did scorched men respond to God's plague?", options:["They blasphemed God and repented not","They cried out for mercy","They tore their clothes in grief","They fell on their faces in worship"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:9",verse:"And men were scorched with great heat, and blasphemed the name of God, which hath power over these plagues: and they repented not to give him glory.", insight:"Pain alone does not make a penitent; a hard heart can burn and still refuse to bend."},
{q:"Where did the fifth angel pour out his vial?", options:["Upon the seat of the beast","Upon the temple of God","Upon the cities of the saints","Upon the armies of the east"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:10",verse:"And the fifth angel poured out his vial upon the seat of the beast; and his kingdom was full of darkness; and they gnawed their tongues for pain,", insight:"Judgment strikes the very throne of rebellion; no seat of power stands above God's reach."},
{q:"What did men do for pain in the beast's darkened kingdom?", options:["They gnawed their tongues","They tore their garments","They beat their breasts","They covered their eyes"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:10",verse:"And the fifth angel poured out his vial upon the seat of the beast; and his kingdom was full of darkness; and they gnawed their tongues for pain,", insight:"A kingdom of darkness produces only self-torment; evil has no comfort to give its own."},
{q:"How did the men answer their pains and their sores?", options:["They blasphemed the God of heaven and repented not","They asked the saints to pray","They begged the beast for help","They sat in silence and mourning"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:11",verse:"And blasphemed the God of heaven because of their pains and their sores, and repented not of their deeds.", insight:"Twice they blaspheme rather than repent; the pattern of the chapter is hardness answered by hardness."},
{q:"Upon what did the sixth angel pour out his vial?", options:["The great river Euphrates","The river Jordan","The river Nile","The river of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:12",verse:"And the sixth angel poured out his vial upon the great river Euphrates; and the water thereof was dried up, that the way of the kings of the east might be prepared.", insight:"The great river of Babylon dries at God's word; He clears the road for His own purposes."},
{q:"Why was the Euphrates dried up?", options:["That the way of the kings of the east might be prepared","To water the wilderness","To reveal hidden treasure","To stop the trade of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:12",verse:"And the sixth angel poured out his vial upon the great river Euphrates; and the water thereof was dried up, that the way of the kings of the east might be prepared.", insight:"God prepares even the roads His enemies will march; nothing moves outside His plan."},
{q:"What came out of the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet?", options:["Three unclean spirits like frogs","Three doves of peace","Three tongues of fire","Three clouds of smoke"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:13",verse:"And I saw three unclean spirits like frogs come out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet.", insight:"Frogs came from Egypt's plagues too; the old deceptions croak again with a new voice."},
{q:"What do the spirits of devils go forth to do?", options:["Gather the kings to the battle of the great day of God Almighty","Seal the foreheads of the saints","Dry up the rivers of the earth","Shut the gates of heaven"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:14",verse:"For they are the spirits of devils, working miracles, which go forth unto the kings of the earth and of the whole world, to gather them to the battle of that great day of God Almighty.", insight:"Hell's miracles only gather its followers to their ruin; Satan's greatest rally ends at God's battlefield."},
{q:"Who is blessed in the warning, 'Behold, I come as a thief'?", options:["He that watcheth, and keepeth his garments","He that sleeps through the night","He that hides from the day","He that trusts in his own strength"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:15",verse:"Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments, lest he walk naked, and they see his shame.", insight:"Watchfulness is the garment of the wise; keep your life ready, for He comes unannounced."},
{q:"How much did every hailstone weigh?", options:["About the weight of a talent","About the weight of a stone","About the weight of a sheaf","About the weight of a bushel"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 16:21",verse:"And there fell upon men a great hail out of heaven, every stone about the weight of a talent: and men blasphemed God because of the plague of the hail; for the plague thereof was exceeding great.", insight:"Heaven's hail falls heavy because the rebellion was heavy; God's measures match man's deeds."}
]}
,{n:17, name:"Mystery, Babylon the Great",
 seal:{ref:"Revelation 17:14",verse:"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful."},
 facts:["Did you know the name on the woman's forehead, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, works like a brand of ownership, marking her as the great seducer of the nations (Revelation 17:5)?","Did you know the chapter explains its own symbols? The seven heads are said outright to be seven mountains, one of the rare times Revelation interprets itself (Revelation 17:9).","Did you know the ten kings end up hating the woman they served, turning on her at God's hidden direction, proof that wicked alliances always devour themselves (Revelation 17:16-17)."],
 questions:[
{q:"Whom did the angel promise to show John the judgment of?", options:["The great whore that sitteth upon many waters","The dragon in the wilderness","The false prophet","The merchants of the earth"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:1",verse:"And there came one of the seven angels which had the seven vials, and talked with me, saying unto me, Come hither; I will shew unto thee the judgment of the great whore that sitteth upon many waters:", insight:"The judgment is shown before the crime is explained; God wants us to know where rebellion ends."},
{q:"Who committed fornication with the woman?", options:["The kings of the earth","The priests of the temple","The shepherds of the field","The fishermen of the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:2",verse:"With whom the kings of the earth have committed fornication, and the inhabitants of the earth have been made drunk with the wine of her fornication.", insight:"Kings traded their crowns for her favors; earthly power bows easily to spiritual seduction."},
{q:"Where did the angel carry John in the spirit?", options:["Into the wilderness","Onto a high mountain","To the temple","Beside the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:3",verse:"So he carried me away in the spirit into the wilderness: and I saw a woman sit upon a scarlet coloured beast, full of names of blasphemy, having seven heads and ten horns.", insight:"Visions of judgment often come in lonely places; God shows hard truths away from the crowd."},
{q:"What was the woman sitting upon?", options:["A scarlet coloured beast","A white horse","A golden throne","A cloud of fire"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:3",verse:"So he carried me away in the spirit into the wilderness: and I saw a woman sit upon a scarlet coloured beast, full of names of blasphemy, having seven heads and ten horns.", insight:"Her power is borrowed from the beast; all her glory rides on something beneath her."},
{q:"What shall the ten horns do to the whore?", options:["Hate her, make her desolate and naked, eat her flesh, and burn her with fire","Crown her queen of the earth","Worship her golden cup","Carry her to the mountains"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:16",verse:"And the ten horns which thou sawest upon the beast, these shall hate the whore, and shall make her desolate and naked, and shall eat her flesh, and burn her with fire.", insight:"Her own allies turn on her; the friendships of sin always end in betrayal."},
{q:"In what colors was the woman arrayed?", options:["Purple and scarlet","Blue and silver","Green and gold","Black and white"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:4",verse:"And the woman was arrayed in purple and scarlet colour, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls, having a golden cup in her hand full of abominations and filthiness of her fornication:", insight:"She wears the colors of royalty and luxury; seduction always dresses above its station."},
{q:"What did the woman hold in her hand?", options:["A golden cup full of abominations","A silver sword","A crown of thorns","A scroll of names"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:4",verse:"And the woman was arrayed in purple and scarlet colour, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls, having a golden cup in her hand full of abominations and filthiness of her fornication:", insight:"A golden cup cannot sweeten what is inside it; wealth gilds corruption but never cures it."},
{q:"What name was written upon her forehead?", options:["MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS","QUEEN OF HEAVEN AND EARTH","THE BRIDE OF THE DRAGON","RULER OF THE NATIONS"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:5",verse:"And upon her forehead was a name written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.", insight:"Her forehead advertises what she is; sin eventually writes its own name where all can read it."},
{q:"With whose blood was the woman drunken?", options:["The blood of the saints and the martyrs of Jesus","The blood of the kings","The blood of the merchants","The blood of the armies"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:6",verse:"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.", insight:"She drinks the blood of God's people as wine; persecution is her pleasure and her proof."},
{q:"How did John react when he saw her?", options:["He wondered with great admiration","He wept aloud","He covered his eyes","He fell down in worship"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:6",verse:"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.", insight:"Even the apostle was stunned; evil's grandeur can dazzle before its judgment is understood."},
{q:"What did the angel promise to tell John?", options:["The mystery of the woman and of the beast","The names of the martyrs","The day of the wedding","The location of the treasure"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:7",verse:"And the angel said unto me, Wherefore didst thou marvel? I will tell thee the mystery of the woman, and of the beast that carrieth her, which hath the seven heads and ten horns.", insight:"Heaven answers honest wonder; God does not leave His servants marveling without meaning."},
{q:"From where shall the beast ascend?", options:["Out of the bottomless pit","Out of the sea","Out of the wilderness","Out of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:8",verse:"The beast that thou sawest was, and is not; and shall ascend out of the bottomless pit, and go into perdition: and they that dwell on the earth shall wonder, whose names were not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, when they behold the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.", insight:"The beast rises from the pit and returns to perdition; evil's journey is a circle, not a climb."},
{q:"Who will wonder at the beast?", options:["They whose names were not written in the book of life","The angels of heaven","The martyrs under the altar","The elders on the thrones"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:8",verse:"The beast that thou sawest was, and is not; and shall ascend out of the bottomless pit, and go into perdition: and they that dwell on the earth shall wonder, whose names were not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, when they behold the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.", insight:"Those without God's mark are impressed by the beast; the book of life changes what amazes you."},
{q:"What are the seven heads?", options:["Seven mountains, on which the woman sitteth","Seven kings of the east","Seven churches of Asia","Seven trumpets of judgment"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:9",verse:"And here is the mind which hath wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains, on which the woman sitteth.", insight:"Scripture decodes its own symbol here; God wants understanding, not confusion, for His people."},
{q:"What is said of the seven kings?", options:["Five are fallen, and one is, and the other is not yet come","All seven reign together","Three are fallen and four remain","They shall reign a thousand years"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:10",verse:"And there are seven kings: five are fallen, and one is, and the other is not yet come; and when he cometh, he must continue a short space.", insight:"Empires rise and fall on God's timetable; five fallen kings are proof that none of them last."},
{q:"Who is the beast that was, and is not?", options:["The eighth, and is of the seven, and goeth into perdition","The first of the kings","The angel of the pit","The prophet of the east"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:11",verse:"And the beast that was, and is not, even he is the eighth, and is of the seven, and goeth into perdition.", insight:"Even numbered among kings, his end is perdition; position cannot rescue a destiny of ruin."},
{q:"What are the ten horns?", options:["Ten kings, which have received no kingdom as yet","Ten cities of the plain","Ten tribes of Israel","Ten angels of wrath"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:12",verse:"And the ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings, which have received no kingdom as yet; but receive power as kings one hour with the beast.", insight:"They rule for only one hour; the briefest power is all that rebellion gets."},
{q:"What shall the ten kings give to the beast?", options:["Their power and strength","Their gold and silver","Their armies and ships","Their crowns and robes"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:13",verse:"These have one mind, and shall give their power and strength unto the beast.", insight:"United evil still serves one master; all rebellion finally pools its strength in one place."},
{q:"How is the Lamb described who overcomes them?", options:["Lord of lords, and King of kings","Prince of the angels","Son of the morning","Judge of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:14",verse:"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.", insight:"The Lamb wins by titles, not by numbers; His name alone outweighs ten kings."},
{q:"Who are with the Lamb in His victory?", options:["They that are called, and chosen, and faithful","The kings of the east","The merchants of Babylon","The armies of the beast"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 17:14",verse:"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.", insight:"Called, chosen, and faithful; three words that mark everyone who stands with Christ."}
]}
,{n:18, name:"Babylon Is Fallen",
 seal:{ref:"Revelation 18:4",verse:"And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues."},
 facts:["Did you know Babylon's fall is announced twice, 'Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen,' echoing Isaiah's earlier prophecy word for word (Revelation 18:2)?","Did you know the merchants' long cargo list ends with 'slaves, and souls of men,' exposing that Babylon's luxury trade dealt in human beings (Revelation 18:13)?","Did you know the millstone thrown into the sea pictures total disappearance? What sinks with a millstone never rises again (Revelation 18:21)."],
 questions:[
{q:"What was the earth lightened with when the angel came down?", options:["His glory","His trumpet","His sword","His chariot"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:1",verse:"And after these things I saw another angel come down from heaven, having great power; and the earth was lightened with his glory.", insight:"One angel's glory lights the whole earth; heaven's messengers outshine every earthly power."},
{q:"What did the angel cry with a strong voice?", options:["Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen","The day of the Lord is come","The seals are opened","The dead are raised"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:2",verse:"And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.", insight:"The fall is announced twice, as certain and complete; God repeats what He wants believed."},
{q:"What had fallen Babylon become?", options:["The habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit","A garden of the Lord","A city of refuge","A holy temple"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:2",verse:"And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.", insight:"Emptied of men, she fills with demons; the city that cast out God inherits worse tenants."},
{q:"Who waxed rich through the abundance of her delicacies?", options:["The merchants of the earth","The priests of the temple","The fishermen of the sea","The farmers of the field"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:3",verse:"For all nations have drunk of the wine of the wrath of her fornication, and the kings of the earth have committed fornication with her, and the merchants of the earth are waxed rich through the abundance of her delicacies.", insight:"Prosperity built on sin enriches many before it ruins all; shared profit is not shared innocence."},
{q:"What did the voice from heaven command God's people?", options:["Come out of her, my people","Go up into her towers","Buy of her merchandise","Hide within her walls"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:4",verse:"And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues.", insight:"'My people' can be inside Babylon; God's call is to separate before the judgment falls."},
{q:"Why must God's people come out of her?", options:["That ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues","To escape the famine","To find better markets","To build a new city"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:4",verse:"And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues.", insight:"Staying means sharing; you cannot dwell in sin's house and escape sin's sentence."},
{q:"How far had her sins reached?", options:["Unto heaven","Unto the sea","Unto the mountains","Unto the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:5",verse:"For her sins have reached unto heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities.", insight:"Sin piles up until it touches heaven; God may wait, but He always remembers."},
{q:"How was Babylon to be rewarded?", options:["Double unto her double, according to her works","A third of her wealth","Seven years of famine","Exile for a generation"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:6",verse:"Reward her even as she rewarded you, and double unto her double according to her works: in the cup which she hath filled fill to her double.", insight:"The cup she filled is returned doubled; God repays in the measure men have used."},
{q:"What did Babylon say in her heart?", options:["I sit a queen, and am no widow, and shall see no sorrow","I am the mother of nations","My walls shall never fall","The gods have blessed me forever"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:7",verse:"How much she hath glorified herself, and lived deliciously, so much torment and sorrow give her: for she saith in her heart, I sit a queen, and am no widow, and shall see no sorrow.", insight:"'I sit a queen' is the proudest sentence in the chapter; pride speaks loudest just before the fall."},
{q:"How quickly shall her plagues come?", options:["In one day","In one year","In one month","In one week"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:8",verse:"Therefore shall her plagues come in one day, death, and mourning, and famine; and she shall be utterly burned with fire: for strong is the Lord God who judgeth her.", insight:"One day undoes what ages built; the swiftness of judgment matches the swiftness of pride."},
{q:"Name the three plagues of that one day.", options:["Death, and mourning, and famine","Fire, hail, and darkness","War, plague, and earthquake","Flood, wind, and locusts"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:8",verse:"Therefore shall her plagues come in one day, death, and mourning, and famine; and she shall be utterly burned with fire: for strong is the Lord God who judgeth her.", insight:"She who knew no sorrow shall know all three sorrows at once; judgment answers boasting precisely."},
{q:"Who shall bewail Babylon when they see the smoke of her burning?", options:["The kings of the earth","The prophets of God","The apostles","The martyrs"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:9",verse:"And the kings of the earth, who have committed fornication and lived deliciously with her, shall bewail her, and lament for her, when they shall see the smoke of her burning,", insight:"Her lovers mourn her, not for her sake but for their lost pleasures; sin is loved only for what it gives."},
{q:"From where did the kings watch her burning?", options:["Standing afar off for the fear of her torment","From the city gates","From their thrones","From the ships at anchor"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:10",verse:"Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas, that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come.", insight:"They loved her near and mourn her far; fear keeps even her friends at a distance."},
{q:"In how long is Babylon's judgment said to come?", options:["In one hour","In one night","In one moment","In one season"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:10",verse:"Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas, that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come.", insight:"'In one hour' is the chapter's drumbeat; what men trust for centuries, God judges in an hour."},
{q:"Why did the merchants weep and mourn over her?", options:["For no man buyeth their merchandise any more","For their ships were burned","For their families were slain","For their gods were broken"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:11",verse:"And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more:", insight:"Their tears are for lost trade, not lost souls; the world's grief is always about its goods."},
{q:"What is the last item in the merchants' cargo list?", options:["Slaves, and souls of men","Spices and perfumes","Horses and chariots","Gold and silver"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:13",verse:"And cinnamon, and odours, and ointments, and frankincense, and wine, and oil, and fine flour, and wheat, and beasts, and sheep, and horses, and chariots, and slaves, and souls of men.", insight:"Her trade ends in human souls; every empire of greed finally sells people."},
{q:"Who stood afar off when the city's riches came to nought?", options:["Every shipmaster, and all the company in ships, and sailors","The kings of the earth","The priests of Babylon","The armies of the east"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:17",verse:"For in one hour so great riches is come to nought. And every shipmaster, and all the company in ships, and sailors, and as many as trade by sea, stood afar off,", insight:"Even the sea captains stop to stare; when great wealth dies, the whole world watches."},
{q:"What did the sailors cry when they saw the smoke of her burning?", options:["What city is like unto this great city","Save us from the fire","Woe to the merchants","The gods have failed"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:18",verse:"And cried when they saw the smoke of her burning, saying, What city is like unto this great city!", insight:"Their wonder is for the city, not for God; amazement at ruin is not repentance."},
{q:"Who is told to rejoice over Babylon?", options:["Thou heaven, and ye holy apostles and prophets","The kings of the earth","The merchants of the sea","The nations round about"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:20",verse:"Rejoice over her, thou heaven, and ye holy apostles and prophets; for God hath avenged you on her.", insight:"Heaven rejoices where earth weeps; the same fall is justice to the saints and loss to the world."},
{q:"What did the mighty angel cast into the sea?", options:["A stone like a great millstone","A golden crown","A burning torch","A broken sword"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 18:21",verse:"And a mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying, Thus with violence shall that great city Babylon be thrown down, and shall be found no more at all.", insight:"A millstone sinks past recovery; Babylon's fall is final, with no rising again."}
]}
,{n:19, name:"The Marriage of the Lamb",
 seal:{ref:"Revelation 19:6",verse:"And I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunderings, saying, Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth."},
 facts:["Did you know 'Alleluia' appears in the New Testament only here in Revelation 19, four times, all in heaven's praise after Babylon's fall (Revelation 19:1, 3, 4, 6)?","Did you know the bride's fine linen is defined right in the text: 'the fine linen is the righteousness of saints' (Revelation 19:8)?","Did you know the Rider bears a written name on His thigh, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS, marking His authority over every earthly ruler (Revelation 19:16)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"What did the great voice of much people in heaven cry?", options:["Alleluia","Hosanna","Holy, holy, holy","Amen"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:1",verse:"And after these things I heard a great voice of much people in heaven, saying, Alleluia; Salvation, and glory, and honour, and power, unto the Lord our God:", insight:"Heaven's first word after Babylon's fall is praise; judgment completed becomes worship begun."},
{q:"What four things are ascribed unto the Lord our God?", options:["Salvation, and glory, and honour, and power","Wisdom, and strength, and riches, and blessing","Mercy, and truth, and grace, and peace","Light, and life, and love, and joy"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:1",verse:"And after these things I heard a great voice of much people in heaven, saying, Alleluia; Salvation, and glory, and honour, and power, unto the Lord our God:", insight:"Salvation heads the list; everything heaven praises begins with what God has saved."},
{q:"Why are God's judgments called true and righteous?", options:["He hath judged the great whore, and avenged the blood of his servants","He hath sealed the saints","He hath opened the temple","He hath silenced the prophets"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:2",verse:"For true and righteous are his judgments: for he hath judged the great whore, which did corrupt the earth with her fornication, and hath avenged the blood of his servants at her hand.", insight:"His judgments are righteous because they answer real wrongs; God avenges, never merely punishes."},
{q:"What rose up for ever and ever?", options:["Her smoke","Her song","Her walls","Her crown"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:3",verse:"And again they said, Alleluia. And her smoke rose up for ever and ever.", insight:"The smoke rises forever as a memorial; some ruins stand as eternal warnings."},
{q:"Who fell down and worshipped God that sat on the throne?", options:["The four and twenty elders and the four beasts","The seven angels","The martyrs","The kings of the earth"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:4",verse:"And the four and twenty elders and the four beasts fell down and worshipped God that sat on the throne, saying, Amen; Alleluia.", insight:"The oldest worshippers lead the newest praise; heaven's elders never tire of 'Amen; Alleluia.'"},
{q:"Whom did the voice out of the throne call to praise God?", options:["All ye his servants, and ye that fear him, both small and great","The angels only","The apostles only","The martyrs only"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:5",verse:"And a voice came out of the throne, saying, Praise our God, all ye his servants, and ye that fear him, both small and great.", insight:"Small and great alike are summoned; in heaven's choir there are no minor voices."},
{q:"What did the voice like many waters and mighty thunderings proclaim?", options:["Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth","The bride is coming","The seals are broken","The dead are judged"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:6",verse:"And I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunderings, saying, Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth.", insight:"Omnipotent means all power is His; every rival throne is a shadow beside this reign."},
{q:"What is come, for which we are to be glad and rejoice?", options:["The marriage of the Lamb","The coronation of the kings","The building of the temple","The gathering of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:7",verse:"Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready.", insight:"After judgment comes a wedding; God's story ends not in ruin but in rejoicing."},
{q:"How had the Lamb's wife made herself ready?", options:["She was arrayed in fine linen, clean and white","She gathered gold and jewels","She built a palace","She called the guests"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:8",verse:"And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints.", insight:"Her readiness is righteousness, not finery; the wedding garment is a holy life."},
{q:"What is the fine linen?", options:["The righteousness of saints","The robes of angels","The curtains of the temple","The banners of the armies"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:8",verse:"And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints.", insight:"Scripture interprets its own symbol: linen is lived holiness, the saints' righteous acts."},
{q:"Who are called blessed in this chapter?", options:["They which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb","They which never sinned","They which built the temple","They which judged the nations"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:9",verse:"And he saith unto me, Write, Blessed are they which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb. And he saith unto me, These are the true sayings of God.", insight:"Blessing is an invitation, not an achievement; the honored guests are simply the called."},
{q:"What did the angel say when John fell at his feet to worship him?", options:["See thou do it not: worship God","Rise, and be blessed","Tell no man","Kneel and be silent"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:10",verse:"And I fell at his feet to worship him. And he said unto me, See thou do it not: I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren that have the testimony of Jesus: worship God: for the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.", insight:"Even the brightest angel refuses worship; all glory detours to God alone."},
{q:"What is the spirit of prophecy?", options:["The testimony of Jesus","The visions of the night","The songs of the elders","The words of the law"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:10",verse:"And I fell at his feet to worship him. And he said unto me, See thou do it not: I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren that have the testimony of Jesus: worship God: for the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.", insight:"All true prophecy points to Jesus; every vision finds its meaning in Him."},
{q:"When heaven opened, what did John see?", options:["A white horse","A golden chariot","A flaming sword","A crystal sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:11",verse:"And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war.", insight:"The white horse means conquest and triumph; Christ returns as the Victor, not the victim."},
{q:"What was the Rider upon the white horse called?", options:["Faithful and True","Mighty and Strong","Holy and Just","Great and Terrible"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:11",verse:"And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war.", insight:"His names are His character; unlike earthly rulers, He is exactly what He is called."},
{q:"What were His eyes like?", options:["As a flame of fire","As the sun at noon","As lightning","As burning coals"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:12",verse:"His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself.", insight:"Flame-eyed, He sees through every disguise; nothing hidden escapes the Rider's gaze."},
{q:"What was on His head?", options:["Many crowns","One crown of gold","A crown of thorns","A helmet of brass"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:12",verse:"His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself.", insight:"Many crowns for many kingdoms; every authority on earth is gathered into His."},
{q:"What is His name called?", options:["The Word of God","The Son of Man","The Bright Morning Star","The Lion of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:13",verse:"And he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God.", insight:"The Word who spoke creation now rides to judge it; the same voice, now in war."},
{q:"What name was written on His vesture and on His thigh?", options:["KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS","FAITHFUL AND TRUE","THE WORD OF GOD","ALMIGHTY GOD"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:16",verse:"And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.", insight:"Written where all can read it; His supremacy is published, not whispered."},
{q:"What happened to the beast and the false prophet?", options:["They were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone","They were bound for a thousand years","They fled into the wilderness","They were sealed in the pit"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 19:20",verse:"And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet that wrought miracles before him, with which he deceived them that had received the mark of the beast, and them that worshipped his image. These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.", insight:"Cast alive, not after death; the deceivers face their end awake, with no escape."}
]}
,{n:20, name:"The Thousand Years",
 seal:{ref:"Revelation 20:11",verse:"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them."},
 facts:["Did you know the angel needs only one chain and one key to bind Satan for a thousand years, showing how easily God restrains the great deceiver (Revelation 20:1-3)?","Did you know those who share in the first resurrection will reign with Christ a thousand years, and the second death has no power over them (Revelation 20:6)?","Did you know the final judgment turns on one book? Whosoever is not found written in the book of life is cast into the lake of fire (Revelation 20:15)."],
 questions:[
{q:"What did the angel coming down from heaven have in his hand?", options:["The key of the bottomless pit and a great chain","A sword and a shield","A trumpet and a vial","A book and a seal"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:1",verse:"And I saw an angel come down from heaven, having the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand.", insight:"Key and chain, not sword and army; God binds the devil with simple authority."},
{q:"Whom did the angel lay hold on?", options:["The dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan","The beast","The false prophet","The great whore"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:2",verse:"And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years,", insight:"Four names for one enemy; Scripture piles up titles to make sure we know exactly who is bound."},
{q:"How long was Satan bound?", options:["A thousand years","A hundred years","Forty years","Seven years"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:2",verse:"And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years,", insight:"A thousand years of silence for the deceiver; God's calendar gives evil a fixed, finished term."},
{q:"Why was Satan shut up and sealed in the pit?", options:["That he should deceive the nations no more","To punish him forever","To hide him from the saints","To keep him until the wedding"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:3",verse:"And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season.", insight:"Deception is his whole trade; take it away and the world finally breathes free."},
{q:"What must happen to Satan after the thousand years?", options:["He must be loosed a little season","He must be judged at once","He must be cast into the sea","He must serve the saints"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:3",verse:"And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season.", insight:"Even the loosing is on God's leash, 'a little season'; evil's last hour is measured too."},
{q:"Whose souls did John see living and reigning with Christ?", options:["Them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God","The kings of the earth","The merchants of Babylon","The builders of the city"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:4",verse:"And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years.", insight:"The beheaded become the enthroned; God repays the martyrs' loss with a reign."},
{q:"What is said of those who had not worshipped the beast?", options:["They lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years","They slept until the end","They served in the temple","They watched from afar"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:4",verse:"And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years.", insight:"Refusing the beast's mark buys a thousand-year crown; faithfulness is never a bad trade."},
{q:"What is the first resurrection?", options:["The rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished","The raising of the martyrs only","The opening of the graves at Jerusalem","The coming of the new heaven"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:5",verse:"But the rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection.", insight:"The chapter itself defines the term; God names the resurrection His people share."},
{q:"What happens to whosoever is not found written in the book of life?", options:["He is cast into the lake of fire","He is given a second trial","He is sent to the wilderness","He is bound for a thousand years"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:15",verse:"And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.", insight:"One book decides the final sentence; make sure your name is written in it."},
{q:"What has no power over those in the first resurrection?", options:["The second death","The lake of fire's smoke","The beast's mark","The pit's darkness"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:6",verse:"Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years.", insight:"One death faced in faith cancels the second forever; the martyrs die once and live always."},
{q:"What shall those of the first resurrection be?", options:["Priests of God and of Christ","Kings of the east","Judges of the angels","Keepers of the gates"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:6",verse:"Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years.", insight:"Priests who reign; service and sovereignty meet in everyone Christ raises."},
{q:"What happens when the thousand years are expired?", options:["Satan shall be loosed out of his prison","The new heaven appears","The saints are judged","The earth is renewed"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:7",verse:"And when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison,", insight:"The last test comes after the long peace; God lets evil show its face one final time."},
{q:"Whom shall Satan go out to deceive?", options:["The nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog","The saints in the camp","The angels of heaven","The kings of the east"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:8",verse:"And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea.", insight:"Gog and Magog, the old names of rebellion, return; evil's last army wears ancient uniforms."},
{q:"How many are gathered for that last battle?", options:["As the sand of the sea","As the stars of heaven","As the locusts of the field","As the drops of rain"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:8",verse:"And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea.", insight:"Numberless as sand, yet gone in a moment; multitudes mean nothing against God."},
{q:"What happened when they compassed the camp of the saints?", options:["Fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them","The earth opened and swallowed them","The sea covered them","The saints fled into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:9",verse:"And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them.", insight:"No battle is even fought; heaven's fire ends the war before the saints lift a hand."},
{q:"Where was the devil cast?", options:["Into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are","Into the bottomless pit","Into the outer darkness","Into the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:10",verse:"And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.", insight:"He joins the company he led; the deceiver shares the doom of his own disciples."},
{q:"What did John see after Satan's doom?", options:["A great white throne, and him that sat on it","A new temple","A golden city","A crystal river"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:11",verse:"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.", insight:"The great white throne is the last sight of the old order; all things end before this seat."},
{q:"What happened before the face of Him on the throne?", options:["The earth and the heaven fled away","The stars fell","The sea dried up","The mountains melted"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:11",verse:"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.", insight:"Heaven and earth flee; when the Judge appears, even creation finds no place to stand."},
{q:"Out of what were the dead judged?", options:["Those things which were written in the books, according to their works","The testimony of the angels","The memories of the saints","The laws of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:12",verse:"And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.", insight:"Written records, not rumors; God's judgment works from evidence, not impression."},
{q:"What is the second death?", options:["Death and hell cast into the lake of fire","The sleep of the soul","The silence of the grave","The darkness of the pit"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 20:14",verse:"And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death.", insight:"Even death dies; the last enemy is unmade in the very fire it served."}
]}
]);
